  "definition": "Overfitting is a phenomenon in machine learning where a model learns the training data too precisely\u2014including noise and spurious correlations\u2014resulting in poor generalisation to unseen data. It corresponds to high variance and low bias in the bias-variance tradeoff, and is mitigated through regularisation, dropout, early stopping, and data augmentation.",
